          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An
            %em Eilenberg–Mac Lane space
            is a connected
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            with nontrivial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            only in a single degree.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#characterization Characterization
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a group, and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            if
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
            %em Eilenberg-MacLane space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,n)
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            with the property that all its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
            are trivial, except that in degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %h3#constructions Constructions
          %h4#via_geometric_realization_of_higher_groupoids Via geometric realization of higher groupoids
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %em Eilenberg–Mac Lane space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,1)
            is the image under the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo :
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo →
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |-| : \infty Grpd \to Top
            of the one-object groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hom-set"} hom-set
            is
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K(G,1) = | \mathbf{B} G |
                  \\,.
          %p
            The construction of EM-spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
            for an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            may be given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dold-Kan+correspondence"} Dold-Kan correspondence
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complexes"} chain complexes
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+abelian+groups"} simplicial abelian groups
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[-n]
            be the chain complex which is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            in dimension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            and zero elsewhere; the geometric realisation of the corresponding simplicial abelian group is then a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
          %p
            We can include the case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            may be nonabelian, by regarding
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(G,n)
            as a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi C
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(C(G,n))
            is then a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=0
            when
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is just a set!) This method also allows for the construction of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi M
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo ;
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(M,n;G,1)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a group, or groupoid, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
            is a
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1 =G
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mi M
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n=M
            all other homotopy trivial, and with the given operation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_1
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_n
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            an abelian group, the Eilenberg–Mac Lane space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
            is the image of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n A
            that is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} strict ∞-groupoid
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathbf{B}^n A]
            that is trivial everywhere except in degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mi n
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mn 1
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo →
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                          %msup
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi n
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                            %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo →
                          %mo *
                          %mo →
                          %mi A
                          %mo →
                          %mo *
                          %mi ⋯
                          %mo →
                          %mo *
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mo →
                          %mo *
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  [\mathbf{B}^n A] &amp;=
                  (  \cdots \to [\mathbf{B}^n A]_{n+1} \to [\mathbf{B}^n A]_{n} \to
                  [\mathbf{B}^n A]_{n-1} \cdots \to [\mathbf{B}^n A]_{1} \stackrel{\to}{\to} [\mathbf{B}^n A]_{0})
                  \\\ &amp;=
                  (  \cdots \to {*} \to A \to
                  {*} \cdots \to {*} \stackrel{\to}{\to} {*})
                  \\end{aligned}
                  \\,.
          %p So
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  K(A,n) = |\mathbf{B}^n A|
                  \\,.
          %p
            Therefore Eilenberg–Mac Lane spaces constitute a
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectrum"} spectrum
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-Mac+Lane+spectrum"} Eilenberg-Mac Lane spectrum
          %p
            In general, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is an abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+group"} topological group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classifying+space"} classifying space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℬ
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}A
            which is an abelian topological group. Iterating this construction, one has a notion of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}^n A
            and a model for it which is an abelian topological group. If moreover
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is discrete, then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℬ
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}A=|\mathbf{B}A|=K(A,1)
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℬ
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{B}^n A=|\mathbf{B}^n A|=K(A,n)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
            which is an abelian topological group.
          %p
            See for instance (
            %a{:href => "#May"}> May, chapter 16, section 5
            )
          %h4#via_linearization_of_spheres Via linearization of spheres
          #ReducedALinearizationOfnSphere.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong
                reduced
                = succeed "-linearization" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[S^n]_\ast
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-sphere"} n-sphere
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
              is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo ⊔
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi k
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi k
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\underset{k \in \mathbb{N}}{\sqcup}
                    A^k \times (S^n)^k
                    \\longrightarrow
                    A[S^n]_\ast
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+abelian+group"} free abelian group
              on the underlying set of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi S
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formal+linear+combination"} formal linear combination
              of the (any fixed) basepoint of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n
              with 0. The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topology
              is the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+topology"} quotient topology
              (of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/disjoint+union"} disjoint union
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product+topological+spaces"} product topological spaces
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is equipped with the
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topology"} discrete topology
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"}> Aguilar-Gitler-Prieto 02, def. 6.4.20
            )
          #ReducedALinearizationOfnSphereIsEMSpace.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/countable+set"} countable
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
              = succeed "-linearization" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[S^n]_\ast
              (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedALinearizationOfnSphere"}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+space"} Eilenberg-MacLane space
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              are
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi q
                              %mo =
                              %mi n
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mo *
                            %mtd
                              %mi otherwise
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_q(A[S^n]_\ast)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    A &amp; if \; q = n
                    \\\
                    \\ast &amp; otherwise
                    }
                    \\right.
            %p
              (in particular for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              then there is a unique connected component and hence we need not specify a basepoint for the homotopy group).
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#AguilarGitlerPrieto02"}> Aguilar-Gitler-Prieto 02, corollary 6.4.23
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The topological space
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A[S^n]_\ast
              in definition
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedALinearizationOfnSphere"}
              has a canonical continuous
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal group
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi O
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O(n)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^n \simeq (\mathbb{R}^n)^\ast
              as the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-point+compactification"} one-point compactification
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ReducedALinearizationOfnSphereIsEMSpace"}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eilenberg-MacLane+spectra"} Eilenberg-MacLane spectra
              as
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+spectra"} orthogonal spectra
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "Eilenberg-Mac+Lane+spectrum#AsSymmetricSpectra"} there
          %h2#cohomology Cohomology
          %h3#with_coefficients_being_emspaces With coefficients being EM-spaces
          %p
            One common use of Eilenberg–Mac Lane spaces is as coefficient objects for “ordinary”
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            (see e.g.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#May"} May, chapter 22
          %p
            The
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            (when
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (generally) is the collection of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy"} homotopy
            classes of maps from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            into
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G,1)
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(A,n)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^1(X,G) = Ho_{Top}(X, K(G,1)) = Ho_{\infty Grpd}(X, \mathbf{B} G)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n(X,A) = Ho_{Top}(X, K(A,n)) = Ho_{\infty Grpd}(X, \mathbf{B}^n A)
                  \\,.
          %p
            Here on the right
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_{Top}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho_{\infty Grpd}
            denotes the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-categories"} (∞,1)-categories
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            and of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
          %p
            Not only the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 0
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi Ho
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_0\mathbf{Top}(X, K(A,n))=Ho_{Top}(X, K(A,n))
            is related to the cohomology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            with coefficients in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi_i\mathbf{Top}(X, K(A,n))
            are, and in the most obvious way: if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a connected CW-complex, then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mi i
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                      %mi Grpd
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^{n-i}(X,A)=\pi_i\mathbf{Top}(X, K(A,n))=\pi_i\mathbf{\infty Grpd}(X, \mathbf{B}^n A),
          %p for any choice of base point on the right hand sides. This fact, which appears to have first been remarked by Thom and Federer, is an immediate consequence of the natural homotopy equivalences
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi Y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega\mathbf{H}(X,Y)\simeq \mathbf{H}(X,\Omega Y)
          %p and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\Omega K(A,n)\simeq K(A,n-1)
          %p
            one has in every
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/loop+space+object"} loop space object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a nonabelian group, Gottlieb proves the following nonabelian analogue of the above result: let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            be a finite dimensional connected CW-complex; for a fixed map
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:X\to K(G,1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_f
            be the centralizer in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi π
                    %mn 1
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G=\pi_1 K(G,1)
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_*(\pi_1(X))
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi K
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi G
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Top}(X,K(G,1))
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(C_f,1)
          %p
            Notice that for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a nonabelian group,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1(X,G)
            is a simple (and the most familiar) example of
            = succeed "." do
